+## ARXIV — commonsense MC (no code/hotpot; domain is science text)
+
+### Single-doc MC accuracy (condition = `doceval`; chance in header)
+
+| Condition | hellaswag (0.25) | boolq (0.50) | openbookqa (0.25) |
+|-----------|:----------------:|:------------:|:-----------------:|
+| doc_causal        | - | - | - |
+| cross_doc_link    | - | - | - |
+| doc_concatenated  | - | - | - |
+| doc_concat_link   | - | - | - |
+
+*(all arxiv models still training)*
+
+### Link-injection MC accuracy (condition = `annotated`; cross_doc_link only)
+
+| Condition | hellaswag | boolq | openbookqa |
+|-----------|:---------:|:-----:|:----------:|
+| cross_doc_link | - | - | - |
+
+### Held-out / community perplexity (BROKEN — graph path)
+
+| Condition | held_out val_random | held_out test_random | community val | community test |
+|-----------|:-------------------:|:--------------------:|:-------------:|:--------------:|
+| doc_causal        | - | - | - | - |
+| cross_doc_link    | - | - | - | - |
+| doc_concatenated  | - | - | - | - |
+| doc_concat_link   | - | - | - | - |
+
+---
+
+## Headline findings so far
+
+- **Cross-doc attention shows real signal** on the two benchmarks built to test
+  it: wiki `hotpotqa_cross_doc` (−14.3% NLL vs flat). thestack
+  `repobench_cross_doc` pending.
+- **thestack doc_causal** is the only model clearly above chance on a discrete
+  benchmark (humaneval_buggy 0.61).
+- **Wiki commonsense MC is at chance** across the board — expected for 1-epoch
+  models; these benchmarks likely need much more training (or aren't the right
+  probe for this corpus).
+- **Graph-path perplexity metric is broken** — blocks the held-out/community
+  perplexity comparison that would otherwise be the cleanest cross-condition
+  signal. Fixing it (see TODOS.md → Eval) is the highest-value eval task.
+

